<title>ITALY: Electrolux cuts to affect Italy -unions.</title>
<headline>Electrolux cuts to affect Italy -unions.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Electrolux's restructuring plan which foresees plant closures and some 12,000 staff cuts will affect its Italian Zanussi unit plants, Italian union officials said.</p>
<p>They said in a statement after a meeting in London with Electrolux managing director Michael Treschow that the group had not named any plants to be hit by the cuts but that Treschow had said &quot;the action will hit all countries&quot; adding that &quot;Italy should not think it is being excluded.&quot;</p>
<p>The union officials' statement said that plants to be affected by the restructuring would start to be informed as from Friday.</p>
<p>Last month, Electrolux chairman Anders Scharp said that no Italian plant closures were envisaged. -- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
